<!doctype html>
<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Sample: Layouts on iPhone</title>
<style>
body{margin:0;padding:20px;background:#eceae6;font:14px/1.45 system-ui,sans-serif;color:#111}
h1{font-size:18px;margin:0 0 4px}p.n{margin:0 0 18px;color:#555;max-width:900px}
.row{display:flex;gap:28px;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:flex-start}
.ph{width:390px}
.ph b{display:block;margin:0 0 8px;font-size:15px}
.ph span{display:block;margin:8px 0 0;color:#444;font-size:13px;max-width:390px}
.ph iframe{display:block;width:390px;height:780px;border:8px solid #111;border-radius:34px;background:#fff}
</style></head><body>
<h1>Layouts section on iPhone (390 wide)</h1>
<p class="n">Same filters in all three: Couples / Family pill and the maximum-length slider, now sized for a thumb. What changes is how you pick one of the layouts. Scroll and tap inside each frame. Plan images and dimensions are still the placeholders the page has today.</p>
<div class="row">
<div class="ph"><b>A &middot; Swipe strip</b><iframe src="sample-range-phone-frame.html?v=2#a" title="A"></iframe><span>Layouts sit in a row of cards under the filters. Swipe sideways, tap one, the plan appears below. Everything stays on one screen.</span></div>
<div class="ph"><b>B &middot; Pick from a sheet</b><iframe src="sample-range-phone-frame.html?v=2#b" title="B"></iframe><span>One button shows the chosen layout. Tapping it slides up a list of all layouts. Keeps the page short; the list is one tap away.</span></div>
<div class="ph"><b>C &middot; Expanding list</b><iframe src="sample-range-phone-frame.html?v=2#c" title="C"></iframe><span>The layouts are stacked rows. Tap one and its plan and dimensions open right under it. Nothing hidden, but longer to scroll.</span></div>
</div></body></html>